6. Rust and JavaScript dependencies

Packaging generates dependencies.txt from locked package sources for the
Linux/macOS host and production frontend. It retains upstream copyright,
license and NOTICE files, including source links for MPL-covered components.
The inventory also includes build/test dependencies; presence in that inventory
does not assert that a component is linked into every artifact.

Linux relies on separately installed desktop libraries, including GTK,
WebKitGTK, gtk-layer-shell and wl-clipboard. Their system packages supply
licenses and sources; they are not copied into the portable directory.
